New strings to add to /workspaces/RevEng/string_diffs/nano/negative_strings.txt: 144, ['Go to the first line of the file', 'Help', 'Reverse the direction of the search', 'Redo the last undone operation', 'Go to previous line', 'Mark text starting from the cursor position', 'Count the number of lines, words, and characters', 'Write File Help Text', 'Go one screenful down', 'Welcome to nano.  For basic help, type Ctrl+G.', 'Paste the contents of cutbuffer at current cursor position', '% C', '%s\t\t %s %s', 'Go just beyond end of paragraph; then of next paragraph', 'Toggle the use of Mac format', 'Toggle backing up of the original file', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', 'Go to the matching bracket', 'Do not convert from DOS/Mac format', 'Push the cursor line to the center, then top, then bottom', 'Insert the next keystroke verbatim', 'Insert File Help Text', 'Main nano help text', 'Run the last recorded macro', 'Insert a tab at the cursor position (or indent marked lines)', 'Undo the last operation', 'Go to next line', ' The previous search string will be shown in brackets after the search prompt.  Hitting Enter without entering any text will perform the previous search.  ', ' Type the name that you wish to save the current file as and press Enter to save the file.', '?0H', 'Replace a string or a regular expression', 'Search forward for a string or a regular expression', 'If you have selected text with the mark and then search to replace, only matches in the selected text will be replaced.', 'a C', 'Toggle the use of DOS format', 'Close buffer without saving it', 'Show cursor in file browser & help text', 'Scroll up one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Toggle the case sensitivity of the search', 'Toggle appending', 'If you need another blank buffer, do not enter any filename, or type in a nonexistent filename at the prompt and press Enter.', ' The following function keys are available in Linter mode:', 'Delete the character to the left of the cursor', ' The following function keys are available in Go To Line mode:', 'Indent the current line (or marked lines)', ' B00 ', 'Go to last row in the viewport', '^0C', 'Go to previous block of text', 'The bottom two lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.', 'Go to the last line of the file', 'Scroll down one line without moving the cursor textually', '!pG', ' In this mode, the status bar shows an error message or warning, and the cursor is put at the corresponding position in the file.  With PageUp and PageDown you can switch to earlier and later messages.', 'Justify the current paragraph', 'Save file without prompting', '"0C', '=== Replacement ===', '0`K', 'Center the line where the cursor is', 'Go to end of current line', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', 'Display this help text', 'Throw away the current line (or marked region)', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', 'Display the position of the cursor', 'If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.', 'a B', ' You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.', 'Unindent the current line (or marked lines)', 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', '--showcursor', 'Toggle prepending', 'Spell Check Help Text', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', '5P2', ' The following function keys are available in Write File mode:', 'Switch to the previous file buffer', ' The spell checker checks the spelling of all text in the current file.  When an unknown word is encountered, it is highlighted and a replacement can be edited.  It will then prompt to replace every instance of the given misspelled word in the current file, or, if you have selected text with the mark, in the selected text.', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Switch to the next file buffer', 'Cancel the current function', 'Go to line and column number', 'Justify the entire file', '\t\t ', ' Enter the line number that you wish to go to and hit Enter.  If there are fewer lines of text than the number you entered, you will be brought to the last line of the file.', '%s                ', 's0 ', 'Go to beginning of paragraph; then of previous paragraph', 'Execute Command Help Text', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', 'Search Command Help Text', 'Go back one character', 'Execute a function or an external command', 'Close the current buffer / Exit from nano', '^ C', 'Go to beginning of current line', 'Go one screenful up', 'Search next occurrence backward', '(%s)       ', 'Toggle the use of regular expressions', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', '\t\t  %s', 'Start/stop recording a macro', ' The following function keys are available at this prompt:', 'Delete the character under the cursor', ' The following function keys are available in Spell Check mode:', '=== Linter ===', 'Go forward one word', '(pg', ':t7', 'nanohelp', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', 'Search next occurrence forward', '" G', " This mode allows you to insert the output of a command run by the shell into the current buffer (or into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' (the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', '!0F', 'enable/disable', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", 'Go To Line Help Text', 'Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.  The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.  Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:', ' The following function keys are available in Search mode:', 'Go to next block of text', 'Go forward one character', '?0G', ' Enter the words or characters you would like to search for, and then press Enter.  If there is a match for the text you entered, the screen will be updated to the location of the nearest match for the search string.', 'Go back one word', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', ' The following function keys are available in Insert File mode:', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', 'b0C', 'Pipe the current buffer (or marked region) to the command', 'Search backward for a string or a regular expression', 'Suspend the editor (return to the shell)', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', '!0G', 'Invoke the spell checker, if available', 'Cut from the cursor position to the end of the file', 'Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Go to first row in the viewport']
