he position of the cursor', 'If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.', 'Nano will be unable to load or save search history or cursor positions.', '--magic', 'a B', ' You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.', 'Unindent the current line (or marked lines)', 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', '--historylog', 'Unable to create directory %s: %s', 'Save & restore position of the cursor', '--showcursor', 'Toggle prepending', 'Spell Check Help Text', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', '5P2', ' The following function keys are available in Write File mode:', 'Switch to the previous file buffer', ' The spell checker checks the spelling of all text in the current file.  When an unknown word is encountered, it is highlighted and a replacement can be edited.  It will then prompt to replace every instance of the given misspelled word in the current file, or, if you have selected text with the mark, in the selected text.', ' B2', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', '0B0p0', 'A0@', ' --disable-linenumbers', ' aR', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Switch to the next file buffer', 'Cancel the current function', 'Go to line and column number', '! B', 'Justify the entire file', '* 0', '__ctype_toupper_loc', 'tdP', ' 0E', ' Enter the line number that you wish to go to and hit Enter.  If there are fewer lines of text than the number you entered, you will be brought to the last line of the file.', '%s                ', '_0[', 's0 ', 'Go to beginning of paragraph; then of previous paragraph', ':42', 'Execute Command Help Text', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', '__uflow', '20C', '300', 'Search Command Help Text', 'Go back one character', ' --disable-color', 'Execute a function or an external command', 'R?D', '!!0', 'Close the current buffer / Exit from nano', '^ C', 'Go to beginning of current line', 'P@0', '  D', 'Go one screenful up', 'Newer', 'Search next occurrence backward', '(%s)       ', 'Toggle the use of regular expressions', '\t D', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', '\t\t  %s', 'Start/stop recording a macro', '[`F', ' The following function keys are available at this prompt:', 'f&F', 'search_history', 'Delete the character under the cursor', ' The following function keys are available in Spell Check mode:', '=== Linter ===', 'JT ', 'Go forward one word', '(pg', ':t7', 'Also try magic to determine syntax', 'It is required for saving/loading search history or cursor positions.', '/.local', 'nanohelp', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', 'a0C', 'Search next occurrence forward', '0@-', '" G', " This mode allows you to insert the output of a command run by the shell into the current buffer (or into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' (the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', '/.nano/', ' --disable-speller', '7 C', '@#b', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', '!0F', '%0F', '!A0', 'A C', 'enable/disable', '+ C', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", 'Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.  The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.  Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:', ' The following function keys are available in Search mode:', "'0G", '00@', 'A3c', '00F', 'Go to next block of text', 'Go forward one character', '?0G', '0 C', ' 0F', 'S9D', ' Enter the words or characters you would like to search for, and then press Enter.  If there is a match for the text you entered, the screen will be updated to the location of the nearest match for the search string.', 'Go back one word', '0aR', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', 'B/@', ' The following function keys are available in Insert File mode:', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', '0bR', 'A?D', 'b0C', 'Pipe the current buffer (or marked region) to the command', '0 A', '_0D', 'Search backward for a string or a regular expression', ' B0', 'Suspend the editor (return to the shell)', 'Go To Line Help Text', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', '!0G', 'Invoke the spell checker, if available', 'U%E', 'Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Go to first row in the viewport'}
