t:\n\n', 890), ('Browser Go To Directory Help Text\n\n "\n\t\t\t\t"Enter the name of the directory you would like to "\n\t\t\t\t"browse to.\n\n If tab completion has not been "\n\t\t\t\t"disabled, you can use the Tab key to (attempt to) "\n\t\t\t\t"automatically complete the directory name.\n\n The "\n\t\t\t\t"following function keys are available in Browser Go "\n\t\t\t\t"To Directory mode:\n\n', 891), ('Browser Go To Directory Help Text\n\n ', 892), ('Enter the name of the directory you would like to ', 893), ('browse to.\n\n If tab completion has not been ', 894), ('disabled, you can use the Tab key to (attempt to) ', 895), ('automatically complete the directory name.\n\n The ', 896), ('following function keys are available in Browser Go ', 897), ('To Directory mode:\n\n', 898), ('Spell Check Help Text\n\n "\n\t\t\t\t"The spell checker checks the spelling of all text in "\n\t\t\t\t"the current file.  When an unknown word is "\n\t\t\t\t"encountered, it is highlighted and a replacement can "\n\t\t\t\t"be edited.  It will then prompt to replace every "\n\t\t\t\t"instance of the given misspelled word in the current "\n\t\t\t\t"file, or, if you have selected text with the mark, in "\n\t\t\t\t"the selected text.\n\n The following function keys "\n\t\t\t\t"are available in Spell Check mode:\n\n', 899), ('Spell Check Help Text\n\n ', 900), ('The spell checker checks the spelling of all text in ', 901), ('the current file.  When an unknown word is ', 902), ('encountered, it is highlighted and a replacement can ', 903), ('be edited.  It will then prompt to replace every ', 904), ('instance of the given misspelled word in the current ', 905), ('file, or, if you have selected text with the mark, in ', 906), ('the selected text.\n\n The following function keys ', 907), ('are available in Spell Check mode:\n\n', 908), ('Execute Command Help Text\n\n "\n\t\t\t\t"This mode allows you to insert the output of a "\n\t\t\t\t"command run by the shell into the current buffer (or "\n\t\t\t\t"into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by \'|\' "\n\t\t\t\t"(the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer "\n\t\t\t\t"(or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ', 909), ('Execute Command Help Text\n\n ', 910), ('This mode allows you to insert the output of a ', 911), ('command run by the shell into the current buffer (or ', 912), ("into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' ", 913), ('(the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer ', 914), ('(or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ', 915), ('If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any "\n\t\t\t\t"command.\n\n You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a "\n\t\t\t\t"large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.\n\n', 916), ('If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any ', 917), ('command.\n\n You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a ', 918), ('large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.\n\n', 919), (' The following function keys "\n\t\t\t\t"are available at this prompt:\n\n', 920), (' The following function keys ', 921), ('are available at this prompt:\n\n', 922), ('=== Linter ===\n\n "\n\t\t\t\t"In this mode, the status bar shows an error message or "\n\t\t\t\t"warning, and the cursor is put at the corresponding "\n\t\t\t\t"position in the file.  With PageUp and PageDown you "\n\t\t\t\t"can switch to earlier and later messages.\n\n', 923), ('=== Linter ===\n\n ', 924), ('In this mode, the status bar shows an error message or ', 925), ('warning, and the cursor is put at the corresponding ', 926), ('position in the file.  With PageUp and PageDown you ', 927), ('can switch to earlier and later messages.\n\n', 928), (' The following function keys are "\n\t\t\t\t"available in Linter mode:\n\n', 929), (' The following function keys are ', 930), ('available in Linter mode:\n\n', 931), ('Main nano help text\n\n "\n\t\t\t\t"The nano editor is designed to emulate the "\n\t\t\t\t"functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text "\n\t\t\t\t"editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  "\n\t\t\t\t"The top line shows the program version, the current "\n\t\t\t\t"filename being edited, and whether or not the file "\n\t\t\t\t"has been modified.  Next is the main editor window "\n\t\t\t\t"showing the file being edited.  The status line is "\n\t\t\t\t"the third line from the bottom and shows important "\n\t\t\t\t"messages.  ', 932), ('Main nano help text\n\n ', 933), ('The nano editor is designed to emulate the ', 934), ('functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text ', 935), ('editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  ', 936), ('The top line shows the program version, the current ', 937), ('filename being edited, and whether or not the file ', 938), ('has been modified.  Next is the main editor window ', 939), ('showing the file being edited.  The status line is ', 940), ('the third line from the bottom and shows important ', 941), ('messages.  ', 942), ('The bottom two lines show the most commonly used "\n\t\t\t\t"shortcuts in the editor.\n\n Shortcuts are written as "\n\t\t\t\t"follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a \'^\' "\n\t\t\t\t"and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or "\n\t\t\t\t"pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are "\n\t\t\t\t"notated with \'M-\' and can be entered using either the "\n\t\t\t\t"Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ', 943), ('The bottom two lines show the most commonly used ', 944), ('shortcuts in the editor.\n\n Shortcuts are written as ', 945), ("follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' ", 946), ('and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or ', 947), ('pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are ', 948), ("notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the ", 949), ('Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ', 950), ('Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a "\n\t\t\t\t"three-digit decimal number from 000 to 255 will enter "\n\t\t\t\